# Risk-accepted findings in the legacy GitBook 3.2.3 engine tree.
# Everything patchable is patched at image build by
# scripts/patch-vulnerable-deps.sh — the entries below have no fix that the
# engine survives (see the script's comments and issue #20).

# immutable 3.8.3 — engine's core data layer. immutable 4.x breaks the
# engine's Record definitions (verified: pages fail to render). Exposure is
# prototype-pollution via untrusted collection input; the engine only feeds
# it book content from the local filesystem.
CVE-2026-59879
CVE-2026-59880

# braces 1.8.5 / 2.3.2 — ReDoS through crafted glob patterns. Glob input
# comes from the book author's own config, not untrusted users. No fixed
# 1.x/2.x exists; braces 3 is incompatible with the chokidar 1.x consumers.
CVE-2024-4068

# ip 1.1.x (nested in the engine's npm, used only by its SOCKS-proxy path,
# which this image never exercises) — upstream never shipped a fixed
# release for this CVE in any version.
CVE-2024-29415

# ---- MEDIUM severity, consciously not patched (below the CRITICAL/HIGH
# ---- gate; documented here for full-severity audits) ----

# request 2.88.2 SSRF-via-redirect — request is archived and never fixed it;
# the engine only requests npm-registry URLs.
CVE-2023-28155

# uuid 3.x insecure randomness — nested in request, which requires the
# uuid/v4 entrypoint that uuid >= 8 removed; used for multipart boundaries.
CVE-2026-41907

# nunjucks 2.x ReDoS — the engine's templating core; nunjucks 3 changes the
# extension API the engine is built on. Templates come from the book author.
CVE-2023-2142

# micromatch <= 3 ReDoS — same rationale and consumer chain (chokidar 1.x)
# as braces above; glob patterns come from the book author.
CVE-2024-4067

# got 6.x UNC-redirect leak — nested dev-path helper; got 11+ is a breaking
# rewrite. The engine fetches only registry URLs.
CVE-2022-33987

# clean-css 1.x ReDoS — v4 changed the minify API the engine calls; CSS
# input is the book author's own stylesheets.
GHSA-wxhq-pm8v-cw75
